# Code flow stays current

- If your change adds, removes, or renames a module, entry point, data file, or call between modules, update `docs/agents/code-flow.md` in the same PR.
- The Mermaid diagrams are mandatory. Update the diagrams in "At a glance" and "Full flow", not only the file map and text.
- Update the `docs/humans/code-flow.md` diagram only if the one-glance picture changed.
- Never replace a diagram with prose.
- `tests/test_code_flow.py` fails when a `server/**/*.py` or `scripts/*.py` path, or a top-level `web/src/` folder, is missing from `docs/agents/code-flow.md`, or when a Mermaid diagram is deleted.

The flow itself lives in `docs/agents/code-flow.md`. Read it there; do not copy it here.
